  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "mrb_vm_exec",
    "file": "mruby/src/vm.c",
    "description": "The bug is in OP_STRCAT handling in mrb_vm_exec: it blindly executes `mrb_str_concat(mrb, regs[a], regs[a+1])` without validating that `regs[a]` is a live String object. With malformed/fuzzed bytecode generated from the input script, register `regs[a]` can hold an invalid/non-object value, which is then cast down the string modification path (`mrb_str_concat` -> `mrb_str_cat_str` -> `mrb_str_cat` -> `mrb_str_modify` -> `mrb_check_frozen`) causing a wild pointer read in `mrb_frozen_p`.",
    "conditions": "Using `mruby_fuzzer`, attacker-controlled source is compiled/executed and can produce VM state where OP_STRCAT runs on corrupted/unexpected register contents. When OP_STRCAT is reached with `regs[a]` not a valid mutable String object, concatenation attempts to modify it and dereferences an invalid RBasic pointer during frozen-check, leading to ASan SEGV."
  },
